D1-BURN-FIX-A3 — production worker.js patch (worklist A3, 2026-11-22)
Status: READY TO APPLY — NOT APPLIED. No deploy is authorized by this file.
Target: ~/workspace/exchange/worker.js (VERSION 0.7.3, 3,479 lines)
Apply with:  cd ~/workspace/exchange && patch -p0 < D1-BURN-FIX-A3.worker-js.patch
         or:  git apply (if run inside a repo checkout of the file)

WHAT IT FIXES (measured, see D1-BURN-FIX-A3.md):
ensureMigrated() runs the full migrate() once per isolate. migrate() is
~84 statements (47 PRAGMA table_info via ensure(), ~31 CREATE ... IF NOT
EXISTS, assorted checks) and ends with an UNINDEXED COUNT over the
append-only evidence_log — a 3,156-row full scan (measured rows_read=3156
via cf.py d1q, 2026-11-23) paid to rediscover that a one-time 2026
backfill finished long ago. Claimant polling is sparse (~540 requests/h),
so isolates churn: fitting the measured D1 analytics on both axes
(read queries/hour AND rows read/hour) puts the cold-isolate share at
~1/3 of requests on 2026-11-22 and ~2/3 on 2026-11-23. That is the burn:
~1.0-1.1M rows/hour against a 5M/day free tier.

THE FIX, three hunks, no behavior change:
1. ensureMigrated() gates on ONE primary-key lookup
   (exchange_config.schema_epoch, 1 row) before paying for migrate().
   migrate() stamps the epoch when it completes. Any schema change MUST
   bump SCHEMA_EPOCH — the constant sits next to ensureMigrated with a
   comment saying so. Fail-open toward migrate(): an unreadable marker
   (e.g. a pre-v0.7 database with no exchange_config table) runs the
   full migrate, exactly as today.
2. Inside migrate(), the backfill check stops scanning evidence_log:
   a marker row in exchange_config (PK read) replaces the COUNT. The
   COUNT runs at most once more — on the first migrate after this
   lands — and writes the marker either way.
3. migrate() gains idx_evidence_log_trigger so any future trigger scan
   (audits, forensics) is indexed instead of a full table scan.

EXPECTED EFFECT (at 2026-11-22/23 traffic):
cold-isolate cost falls from ~84 read queries / ~3,157 rows to
2 read queries / 2 rows (epoch lookup + ballot_policy check inside
migrate is skipped too — migrate does not run at all). Projected daily
rows read: ~5.0-5.7M -> ~0.3-0.5M (claim path ~34 rows/poll, cron
~4-8k rows/run, completions + gauntlets), i.e. ~10x under the free cap.

NOT IN THIS PATCH (deliberate):
- warrantedTierInfo's lifetime COUNTs (execOk / freeExec). They cost
  ~1,789 rows for nim-nvidia per computation and grow with history, but
  windowing them changes evidence semantics — that is the deep-dive G4
  decision, Zack's call, not a burn patch's.
- /v1/health COUNT(*) scans (709 rows/call). Low call frequency; not
  the burner. Left alone to keep this patch minimal and reviewable.

